          "question": {
            "text": "A carrier wave of peak voltage 16 volt is used to transmit a signal. If the\nmodulation index is $75 \\%$, the peak voltage of the modulating signal is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "WgVp4",
              "text": "6 volt",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "pheYM",
              "text": "24 volt",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "nqwSI",
              "text": "18 volt",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "mCP2B",
              "text": "12 volt",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "A carrier wave of peak voltage $16 \\mathrm{~V}$ is used to transmit a signal. If the modulation index is $75 \\%$, the peak voltage of the modulating signal is $12 \\mathrm{~V}$.\nExplanation:\nModulation Index\n$(\\mathrm{MI})=\\frac{\\text { Peak voltage of modulating signal }\\left(\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{m}}\\right)}{\\text { Peak voltage of carrier } \\operatorname{signal}\\left(\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{C}}\\right)}$\nGiven, $\\mathrm{Ml}=75 \\%$ and $\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{C}}=16 \\mathrm{~V}$\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{m}}=\\mathrm{MI} \\times \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{c}}=\\frac{75}{100} \\times 16=12 \\mathrm{~V}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
