          "question": {
            "text": "In amplitude modulation, the amplitude of carrier wave is <math><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></math> and that of the modulating signal is <math><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> In practice, the ratio of <math><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></math> to <math><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></math> is kept less than or equal to one, to avoid",
